# File structure

## Layers (authoring app)

| Area | Role |
|------|------|
| **`src/pages/`** | Route screens: dashboard, editor shell, not-found |
| **`src/router/`** | React Router **createBrowserRouter** + route modules |
| **`src/components/`** | Shared UI (`ui/`), layout/providers, ErrorBoundary |
| **`src/features/editor/`** | **Canvas editor**: Konva, commands, history, overlays, editor UI |
| **`src/services/api/`** | **docsService** + **IndexedDB** persistence |
| **`src/shared/`** | Shared styles/utils used across app |
| **`src/lib/`** | **`cn()`** / small helpers (e.g. shadcn utils) |
| **`src/hooks/`** | App-level hooks; **`hooks/query/`** for TanStack Query when added |
| **`src/libs/axios/`** | HTTP client + interceptors |

## Do

- Keep **`@/`** alias aligned between **`vite.config.ts`** and **`tsconfig.app.json`**.
- Route constants live in **`src/constants/paths.ts`** (`/dashboard`, `/editor/:docId`).
- Editor mutations go through **`features/editor/core/commands/**`** and **`stores/docStore`** — don’t bypass without a strong reason.

## Don't

- Don’t move editor core types/commands into **`src/pages`** or **`src/components`** root — keep them under **`features/editor`**.
- Don’t commit **`.env`** secrets; placeholders only in samples.

## Barrel files

- Use **`index.ts`** at stable boundaries (`constants`, `hooks/query`, `services`) sparingly; prefer explicit imports for large editor modules when it aids tree-shaking and clarity.

## Scope

Rules target **`new-authoringtool/`** (not the Next.js app at repo root unless explicitly requested).
